45150866072577,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":-0.4063689784847518,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":1.0,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":100.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.0013181689367914723,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":32.9,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.6752254163478884,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":0.0076002206081121956,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":57.6,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.020943132032963534,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":34.4,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.03508774463157074,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":41.5,"_gate_insider_own":0.12979999,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":86.5,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"EverQuote, Inc. operates an online marketplace for insurance shopping in the United States. The company provides automotive, and home and renters insurance, as well as campaign management tools. The company serves insurance carriers and agents, and indirect distributors. The company was formerly known as AdHarmonics, Inc., and changed its name to EverQuote, Inc. in November 2014. EverQuote, Inc. was incorporated in 2008 and is based in Cambridge, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jayme  Mendal | President, CEO & Director | Age 39 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 356 people. Revenue per employee of $1.9M ranks in the top quartile among Communication Services peers, with revenue growing 23%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $254K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $68K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["EverQuote, Inc. is a small-cap communication services business with a $1.0B market cap on $693M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +20% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +2.4pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -31% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $90M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 13 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.96\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin -69.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 13% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (27.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Communication Services peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Advertising-cycle exposure and content/regulatory risk \u2014 a single platform policy shift or ad-spend contraction cascades through the P&L quickly.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cord-cutting acceleration and audience fragmentation \u2014 legacy distribution bundles unravel faster than subscription revenue can replace them.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 23% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Growing faster than most Communication Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Communication Services \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Why EverQuote (EVER) is a Top Growth Stock for the Long-Term","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028124/why-everquote-ever-is-a-top-growth-stock-for-the-long-term?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Czacks_education_growth_score-3028124","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794428226.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Liquidity Mapping Around (EVER) Price Events","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.c